.\" umount.1 -- maux's umount(1), in the V7 man(1) shape. An
.\" original page (this project's own text), so it carries no
.\" third-party notice -- MIT like the code, same posture as tty.1.
.\" Rendered at build time to build/man/UMOUNT.TXT and staged on the
.\" play image as /usr/man/UMOUNT: `man umount`.
.TH UMOUNT 1 "October 10, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
umount \- unmount a floppy or a disk image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B umount
.I /mnt/NAME
.br
.B umount
.I /dev/sNdM
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Umount
takes a Disk ][ that
.IR mount (1)
mounted back out of
.BR /mnt ,
.IR df (1)
and
.IR mount 's
listing. Nothing reads the drive again until it is mounted again.
.PP
It also detaches a disk image that
.IR mount (1)
attached as
.BR /dev/s3d2 :
the unit and its volume go away, the image file is closed and can be
changed again. A volume that holds a mounted image cannot be
unmounted until the image is. If a write to the image failed while it
was mounted (a read-only mount, or the host refusing), the unit is
still detached but
.I umount
says "N blocks were not written" and exits 1.
.PP
The volume is named by its place under
.B /mnt
or by its unit. A name is found by reading, with one ON_LINE each,
only the units already mounted; a drive that is not mounted is never
polled.
.PP
Refused as "busy" while a file on the volume is open or parked, a
process has its working directory on it, or a block device on the
unit is open. The boot volume and fast units (SmartPort, hard disk)
cannot be unmounted: "not a mountable unit".
.SH FILES
/mnt/NAME       a mounted volume
.br
/dev/sNdM       the units
.SH "SEE ALSO"
mount(1), df(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 on success, 1 on failure ("busy", "not mounted",
"not a mountable unit") or when writes to a detached image were lost,
2 for a usage error.
